{"run_id": "20261010T203329_1535fb87", "stage": "first_pass", "question": "When did Duke Kunshan University's four-year undergraduate bachelor's program begin?", "answer": "Duke Kunshan University's four-year undergraduate bachelor's program began in August 2018 [dku-about::c000].", "evidence": "Duke Kunshan University (DKU) is a liberal arts and research university in Kunshan, Jiangsu, China. It was established in September 2013 as a U.S.-China partnership between Duke University and Wuhan University.\n\nDKU welcomed its first students in August 2014, beginning with Duke graduate degrees and a Global Learning Semester. The four-year undergraduate bachelor's program began in August 2018.\n\ng Semester. The four-year undergraduate bachelor's program began in August 2018.\n\nThe campus covers 200 acres in Kunshan's Yangcheng Lake Science and Technology Park. The street address is No. 8 Duke Avenue, Kunshan, Jiangsu Province, China 215316.\n\nThis note is a short local summary of public facts. It does not list tuition, enrollment headcounts, or the names of current officers.\n\nSource: https://www.dukekunshan.edu.cn/about/welcome-to-duke-kunshan-university/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)\n\nDuke University, Durham, North Carolina (not the Kunshan campus)\n\nDuke University's home campus is in Durham, North Carolina, United States, on nearly 9,000 acres. Duke traces its roots to 1838 and officially became Duke University in 1924. Duke enrolls more than 15,000 students in undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs.\n\ndescribed on Duke's international activity list alongside Duke-NUS in Singapore.\n\nSource: https://www.dukekunshan.edu.cn/about/welcome-to-duke-kunshan-university/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "dku", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203115/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "recovery_trigger", "item": 8}
