"judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "dku", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203115/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 16}
{"run_id": "20261010T203309_2d1687a7", "stage": "final", "question": "What is the South Jetty Teaching Lab's lab code?", "answer": "The South Jetty Teaching Lab's lab code is SJ-07 [south-jetty-lab::c000].", "evidence": "South Jetty Teaching Lab booking rules\n\nThe lab code is SJ-07. Undergraduate project groups may book up to two 2-hour slots per day. Slots start at 10:00, 14:00, and 18:00, and the lab does open on Saturdays.\n\nA booking is cancelled if no member taps in with a student card within 10 minutes of the start time. Safety glasses are required at all times inside the wet bench area, powered or not.\n\nNorth Jetty Teaching Lab booking rules\n\nThe lab code is NJ-12. Undergraduate project groups may book at most one 3-hour slot per day. Slots start at 09:00, 13:00, and 16:30 on weekdays only.\n\nA booking is cancelled if no member taps in with a student card within 15 minutes of the start time. Safety glasses are required whenever the soldering bench is powered.\n\nety glasses are required at all times inside the wet bench area, powered or not.\n\nThe lab manager is Dev Okonkwo (dev.okonkwo@harbor-institute.example). There is no overnight access at South Jetty under any circumstances; the building is locked at 21:00.\n\nteen, Gatehouse. North Jetty Lab and Staff Housing are not served during recess.\n\nA single ride still costs 1 harbor credit. Recess day passes are sold at the Gatehouse only, and the Gatehouse desk itself opens at 07:45.\n\nRecess dates are published by the department office each year and are not listed here.", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "harbor", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203121/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 17}
{"run_id": "20261010T203550_01bad4ba", "stage": "first_pass", "question": "How many hours ahead must a group room at the Saltmarsh Annex Library be booked?", "answer": "A group room at the Saltmarsh Annex Library cannot be booked because there are no group rooms available there. Readers who need a group room should book at the Harbor Desk instead [saltmarsh-annex-library::c000]. At the Harbor Institute Library, group rooms must be booked at least two hours ahead [harbor-library::c000].", "evidence": "Saltmarsh Annex Library hours (term time)\n\nMonday to Friday: 09:00–17:00\nSaturday: closed\nSunday: 12:00–18:00\n\nThe Annex is a separate building from the Harbor Institute Library and keeps its own schedule. The quiet study floor here is Level 2. There are no group rooms; readers who need one should book at the Harbor Desk instead.\n\nThe late-return fine at the Annex is 1 harbor credit per day, capped at 25 credits per item. Bottled water and covered cups are both allowed.\n\nHarbor Institute Library hours (term time)\n\nMonday to Thursday: 08:00–21:00\nFriday: 08:00–18:00\nSaturday: 10:00–16:00\nSunday: closed\n\nThe quiet study floor is Level 3. Group rooms on Level 1 must be booked in the Harbor Desk app at least two hours ahead. Food is not allowed except bottled water.\n\nThe late-return fine is 2 harbor credits per day, capped at 40 credits per item. Course reserves cannot leave the building.\n\nSouth Jetty Teaching Lab booking rules\n\nThe lab code is SJ-07. Undergraduate project groups may book up to two 2-hour slots per day. Slots start at 10:00, 14:00, and 18:00, and the lab does open on Saturdays.\n\nA booking is cancelled if no member taps in with a student card within 10 minutes of the start time. Safety glasses are required at all times inside the wet bench area, powered or not.\n\nNorth Jetty Teaching Lab booking rules\n\nThe lab code is NJ-12. Undergraduate project groups may book at most one 3-hour slot per day. Slots start at 09:00, 13:00, and 16:30 on weekdays only.\n\nA booking is cancelled if no member taps in with a student card within 15 minutes of the start time. Safety glasses are required whenever the soldering bench is powered.", "judge_sufficient": false, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "harbor", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203121/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "recovery_trigger", "item": 18}
{"run_id": "20261010T203429_97851bb5", "stage": "first_pass", "question": "According to the August 2021 DKU student handbook, where is the DKU Library located?", "answer": "According to the August 2021 DKU student handbook, the DKU Library is located in two rooms on the first and second floor of the Academic Building [dku-library-handbook-2021::c001].", "evidence": "as historical text. It does not describe the current dedicated library building.\n\nIn this 2021 handbook, the DKU Library is described as occupying two rooms on the first and second floor of the Academic Building. The listed phone number is (0512) 3665-7027. The listed email is dkulibrary@dukekunshan.edu.cn. The handbook also mentions a joint service relationship with Duke University Libraries (DUL).\n\nDKU Library — August 2021 student handbook (superseded)\n\nThis extract is from an August 2021 DKU Student Handbook. It is kept as historical text. It does not describe the current dedicated library building.\n\nDKU Library Guide (January 2025 brochure)\n\nThis document copies service hours and space facts from the January 2025 DKU Library Guide PDF. Where it disagrees with the later Locations & Hours website, treat the website as current and this brochure as dated January 2025.\n\nLibrary building: Monday-Sunday 08:00-23:00. Side gates use swipe access. The guide lists 23 self and group study rooms and 560 seats.\n\nalso mentions a joint service relationship with Duke University Libraries (DUL).\n\nDo not use these 2021 room locations or this 2021 phone number as the current library location or current service desk number.\n\nSource: DKU Student Handbook dated 21.08.19, archived copy at https://sites.nicholas.duke.edu/imep-dku/files/2023/04/21.08.19DKU-Student-Handbook.pdf (retrieved 2026-09-10)", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "dku", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203115/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "recovery_trigger", "item": 19}
