{"run_id": "20261010T203501_f9592145", "stage": "final", "question": "About how much does a taxi from Kunshan South Station to the DKU campus cost according to the International Students Zone note?", "answer": "According to the International Students Zone note, a taxi from Kunshan South Station to the DKU campus costs around 30 RMB [getting-to-dku::c001].", "evidence": "s costing around 30 RMB (from the International Students Zone pre-arrival note).\n\nThis note does not publish a current weekday campus-shuttle timetable from Kunshan South, and it does not list taxi fares from PVG.\n\nSource: https://commencement.dukekunshan.edu.cn/plan-your-visit/ and https://campus-life.dukekunshan.edu.cn/pre-arrival-and-orientation/international-students-zone/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)\n\nGetting to Duke Kunshan University\n\nShanghai Pudong International Airport (PVG) is 92 kilometers east of Kunshan. Shanghai Hongqiao International Airport (SHA) is 42 kilometers east of Kunshan. Sunan Shuofang International Airport (WUX) is 41 kilometers west of Kunshan. Kunshan South Railway Station is 12 kilometers southeast of Duke Kunshan.\n\nFrom Kunshan South Station, a taxi to campus is described as costing around 30 RMB (from the International Students Zone pre-arrival note).\n\nDuke Kunshan University Conference Center\n\nThe Conference Center is on the DKU campus in Kunshan. It has over 200 guest rooms, a gym, and on-campus parking. The auditorium holds up to 300 guests. The grand ballroom can be divided into two rooms.\n\nDining venues named for Conference Center guests include the Conference Center Restaurant, Executive Dining Restaurant, and Water Pavilion. A campus restaurant and a Family Mart in the Community Center are also mentioned.\n\ng Semester. The four-year undergraduate bachelor's program began in August 2018.\n\nThe campus covers 200 acres in Kunshan's Yangcheng Lake Science and Technology Park. The street address is No. 8 Duke Avenue, Kunshan, Jiangsu Province, China 215316.\n\nThis note is a short local summary of public facts. It does not list tuition, enrollment headcounts, or the names of current officers.\n\nSource: https://www.dukekunshan.edu.cn/about/welcome-to-duke-kunshan-university/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "dku", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203115/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 21}
{"run_id": "20261010T202952_d0b038aa", "stage": "final", "question": "What are Shift A hours at Kestrel Aero?", "answer": "Shift A hours at Kestrel Aero are from 06:00 to 14:30 [shifts::c000].", "evidence": "Kestrel Aero Components — about (fictional shop)\n\nKestrel Aero Components is a made-up job shop in the invented town of Red Mesa. It is not a real aerospace supplier.\n\nHangar 2 machines titanium. Shop 6 machines aluminum. The traveler office is in Hangar 2, bay C.\n\nShift board\n\nShift A: 06:00-14:30. Shift B: 14:30-23:00. There is no third shift. The tool crib is staffed on Shift A only.\n\nFay Aerospace (sister shop, not Kestrel)\n\nFay Aerospace is a made-up composites shop across the highway. Its only mill is a 3-axis router. Fay does not hold lot KX-441.\n\nDo not treat Fay hours or specs as Kestrel's.\n\nKestrel contacts\n\nTraveler desk: 555-2201. Quality office: 555-2202. Email: travelers@kestrel-aero.example\n\nOfficer names are omitted on purpose.", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "kestrel", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T202849/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 22}
