{"run_id": "20261010T203421_b5d46558", "stage": "final", "question": "What are the Harbor Institute Library's current Saturday hours?", "answer": "The Harbor Institute Library's current Saturday hours are 10:00 to 16:00 [harbor-library::c000].", "evidence": "Harbor Institute Library hours (term time)\n\nMonday to Thursday: 08:00–21:00\nFriday: 08:00–18:00\nSaturday: 10:00–16:00\nSunday: closed\n\nThe quiet study floor is Level 3. Group rooms on Level 1 must be booked in the Harbor Desk app at least two hours ahead. Food is not allowed except bottled water.\n\nThe late-return fine is 2 harbor credits per day, capped at 40 credits per item. Course reserves cannot leave the building.\n\nSUPERSEDED NOTICE — Harbor Institute Library, East Wing renovation 2019\n\nRetained for records only. These hours were replaced when the renovation finished in December 2019 and do not describe current service. For current hours see the term-time hours sheet.\n\nRenovation hours in effect March–December 2019:\n\nMonday to Thursday: 10:00–16:00\nFriday: 10:00–14:00\nSaturday: 12:00–15:00\nSunday: closed\n\nSaltmarsh Annex Library hours (term time)\n\nMonday to Friday: 09:00–17:00\nSaturday: closed\nSunday: 12:00–18:00\n\nThe Annex is a separate building from the Harbor Institute Library and keeps its own schedule. The quiet study floor here is Level 2. There are no group rooms; readers who need one should book at the Harbor Desk instead.\n\nThe late-return fine at the Annex is 1 harbor credit per day, capped at 25 credits per item. Bottled water and covered cups are both allowed.\n\nHarbor Institute shuttle loop\n\nThe campus shuttle is named the Tideline. On weekdays it runs every 12 minutes from 07:30 to 19:30. Weekend service is every 25 minutes from 09:00 to 17:00.\n\nStops in order: Gatehouse, Library Plaza, North Jetty Lab, Tide Canteen, Staff Housing, Gatehouse.\n\nA single ride costs 1 harbor credit. Faculty and students tap the same blue card used for the library. Visitors buy a paper day pass at the Gatehouse, not on the bus.", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "harbor", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203121/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 28}
{"run_id": "20261010T203330_2cc2c7ed", "stage": "first_pass", "question": "At the North Jetty Teaching Lab, how long is a booking held before it is cancelled if nobody taps in?", "answer": "At the North Jetty Teaching Lab, a booking is cancelled if no member taps in with a student card within 15 minutes of the start time [north-jetty-lab::c000].", "evidence": "South Jetty Teaching Lab booking rules\n\nThe lab code is SJ-07. Undergraduate project groups may book up to two 2-hour slots per day. Slots start at 10:00, 14:00, and 18:00, and the lab does open on Saturdays.\n\nA booking is cancelled if no member taps in with a student card within 10 minutes of the start time. Safety glasses are required at all times inside the wet bench area, powered or not.\n\nNorth Jetty Teaching Lab booking rules\n\nThe lab code is NJ-12. Undergraduate project groups may book at most one 3-hour slot per day. Slots start at 09:00, 13:00, and 16:30 on weekdays only.\n\nA booking is cancelled if no member taps in with a student card within 15 minutes of the start time. Safety glasses are required whenever the soldering bench is powered.\n\nety glasses are required at all times inside the wet bench area, powered or not.\n\nThe lab manager is Dev Okonkwo (dev.okonkwo@harbor-institute.example). There is no overnight access at South Jetty under any circumstances; the building is locked at 21:00.\n\nteen, Gatehouse. North Jetty Lab and Staff Housing are not served during recess.\n\nA single ride still costs 1 harbor credit. Recess day passes are sold at the Gatehouse only, and the Gatehouse desk itself opens at 07:45.\n\nRecess dates are published by the department office each year and are not listed here.", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "harbor", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203121/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "recovery_trigger", "item": 29}
{"run_id": "20261010T203504_de532d7f", "stage": "final", "question": "How many hours did the 1921 Green Lamp Flood last according to the Storm Ledger Unit?", "answer": "According to the Coastal Memory Group, the 1921 \"Green Lamp Flood\" lasted 31 hours in Harbor Town, not 48 hours as previously stated on older tourist plaques [coastal-memory-group::c001].", "evidence": "8 digitized logbooks from 1912–1938. The group does not hold records after 1940.\n\nLead archivist: Jonah Hale. Student liaison: Mei Zhao. External interview requests go to memory@harbor-institute.example, not to personal inboxes.\n\nThe group’s public fact sheet states that the 1921 “Green Lamp Flood” lasted 31 hours in Harbor Town, not 48. That correction is deliberate; older tourist plaques are wrong.\n\nte and are the unit's most requested series. The unit holds nothing before 1940.\n\nLead archivist: Ana Ferreira. Student liaison: Tom Baptiste. Interview requests go to ledger@harbor-institute.example.\n\nThe unit's fact sheet records that the 1948 \"Black Mast Gale\" lasted 19 hours in Harbor Town. The unit does not hold material on the 1921 Green Lamp Flood and refers those enquiries elsewhere.\n\nStorm Ledger Unit (fictional research unit)\n\nThe Storm Ledger Unit studies mid-century harbor weather reporting. The unit office is Room 108 in the West Archive wing. Weekly seminar: Tuesday 10:00–11:00 in Seminar Hut A.\n\nThe unit's holdings cover 1940–1975 and include 214 digitized station reports. Records for 1955 are complete and are the unit's most requested series. The unit holds nothing before 1940.\n\nCoastal Memory Group (fictional research unit)\n\nThe Coastal Memory Group studies how harbor towns archive storm records. The group office is Room 214 in the East Archive wing. Weekly seminar: Thursday 16:00–17:00 in Seminar Hut B.\n\nCurrent working corpus (internal nickname: Salt Ledger) contains 48 digitized logbooks from 1912–1938. The group does not hold records after 1940.", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "harbor", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203121/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 30}
{"run_id": "20261010T203537_0657c86a", "stage": "first_pass", "question": "What time does breakfast end at Halal Dining at the Conference Center?", "answer": "I do not know based on the retrieved documents.", "evidence": "Campus dining — Conference Center Halal Dining\n\nHalal Dining @ Conference Center:\nLunch 11:00-13:30\nDinner 17:00-19:30\n\nNo breakfast hours are listed for Halal Dining at the Conference Center.\n\nThis venue is not University Dining in the Academic Building. It does not list prices.\n\nSource: https://commencement.dukekunshan.edu.cn/plan-your-visit/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)\n\nCampus dining — Academic Building\n\nThree dining halls on campus serve Chinese, Western, and Halal dishes. This note covers only the two Academic Building venues.\n\nUniversity Dining @ Academic Building:\nBreakfast 07:00-09:30\nLunch 11:00-13:30\nDinner 17:00-19:30\n\nExecutive Dining @ Academic Building:\nLunch 11:00-13:30\nNo breakfast hours and no dinner hours are listed for Executive Dining.\n\nThis note does not list menu prices, meal-plan costs, or dish names.\n\ncampus restaurant and a Family Mart in the Community Center are also mentioned.\n\nThis note does not list room rates, a weekday shuttle timetable, or Halal Dining meal times (those times are on the commencement dining note).\n\nSource: https://www.dukekunshan.edu.cn/conference-center/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)\n\nDuke Kunshan University Conference Center\n\nThe Conference Center is on the DKU campus in Kunshan. It has over 200 guest rooms, a gym, and on-campus parking. The auditorium holds up to 300 guests. The grand ballroom can be divided into two rooms.\n\nDining venues named for Conference Center guests include the Conference Center Restaurant, Executive Dining Restaurant, and Water Pavilion. A campus restaurant and a Family Mart in the Community Center are also mentioned.", "judge_sufficient": false, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "dku", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203115/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "recovery_trigger", "item": 31}
{"run_id": "20261010T203340_781e00bd", "stage": "final", "question": "According to the current DKU Library Locations and Hours page, what are the 1st floor information desk hours on Saturday?", "answer": "The 1st floor information desk hours on Saturday are from 14:00 to 21:00 [dku-library-hours::c000].", "evidence": "DKU Library — current locations and hours\n\nThese hours are the current regular schedule published on the DKU Library website. Holiday hours are announced separately and are not listed here.\n\nLibrary building: 08:00-23:00, Monday through Sunday.\n\n1st floor information desk:\nMonday-Friday: 09:00-21:00\nSaturday-Sunday: 14:00-21:00\n\nDVD and equipment loan: Monday-Friday, 09:00-17:30.\n\nDKU Library Guide (January 2025 brochure)\n\nThis document copies service hours and space facts from the January 2025 DKU Library Guide PDF. Where it disagrees with the later Locations & Hours website, treat the website as current and this brochure as dated January 2025.\n\nLibrary building: Monday-Sunday 08:00-23:00. Side gates use swipe access. The guide lists 23 self and group study rooms and 560 seats.\n\nas historical text. It does not describe the current dedicated library building.\n\nIn this 2021 handbook, the DKU Library is described as occupying two rooms on the first and second floor of the Academic Building. The listed phone number is (0512) 3665-7027. The listed email is dkulibrary@dukekunshan.edu.cn. The handbook also mentions a joint service relationship with Duke University Libraries (DUL).\n\naturday-Sunday: 14:00-21:00\n\nDVD and equipment loan: Monday-Friday, 09:00-17:30.\n\nContact:\n(+86) 0512-36658756 (Monday-Friday, 09:00-17:00)\ndkulibrary@dukekunshan.edu.cn\nNo. 8 Duke Avenue, Kunshan, Jiangsu Province, China 215316\n\nThis page is about the Kunshan campus library. It is not Duke University Libraries in Durham, North Carolina.\n\nSource: https://library.dukekunshan.edu.cn/locations-hours/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "dku", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203115/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 32}
{"run_id": "20261010T203305_2a86f26c", "stage": "final", "question": "What is the campus shuttle called?", "answer": "The campus shuttle is called the Tideline [tideline-shuttle::c000].", "evidence": "Harbor Institute shuttle loop\n\nThe campus shuttle is named the Tideline. On weekdays it runs every 12 minutes from 07:30 to 19:30. Weekend service is every 25 minutes from 09:00 to 17:00.\n\nStops in order: Gatehouse, Library Plaza, North Jetty Lab, Tide Canteen, Staff Housing, Gatehouse.\n\nA single ride costs 1 harbor credit. Faculty and students tap the same blue card used for the library. Visitors buy a paper day pass at the Gatehouse, not on the bus.\n\nTideline shuttle: winter recess schedule\n\nDuring winter recess the Tideline runs a reduced loop: every 30 minutes from 08:00 to 18:00, every day including weekends. Normal term-time frequencies do not apply during recess.\n\nThe recess loop skips two stops. Stops served: Gatehouse, Library Plaza, Tide Canteen, Gatehouse. North Jetty Lab and Staff Housing are not served during recess.\n\nfor the library. Visitors buy a paper day pass at the Gatehouse, not on the bus.\n\nThere is no shuttle stop at the boat museum. Walk 8 minutes from Library Plaza if you need that building.\n\nteen, Gatehouse. North Jetty Lab and Staff Housing are not served during recess.\n\nA single ride still costs 1 harbor credit. Recess day passes are sold at the Gatehouse only, and the Gatehouse desk itself opens at 07:45.\n\nRecess dates are published by the department office each year and are not listed here.", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "harbor", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203121/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 33}
{"run_id": "20261010T203403_01efe296", "stage": "final", "question": "What are DVD and equipment loan hours at the DKU Library according to the current Locations and Hours page?", "answer": "The DVD and equipment loan hours at the DKU Library are Monday to Friday, from 09:00 to 17:30 [dku-library-hours::c000].", "evidence": "DKU Library — current locations and hours\n\nThese hours are the current regular schedule published on the DKU Library website. Holiday hours are announced separately and are not listed here.\n\nLibrary building: 08:00-23:00, Monday through Sunday.\n\n1st floor information desk:\nMonday-Friday: 09:00-21:00\nSaturday-Sunday: 14:00-21:00\n\nDVD and equipment loan: Monday-Friday, 09:00-17:30.\n\naturday-Sunday: 14:00-21:00\n\nDVD and equipment loan: Monday-Friday, 09:00-17:30.\n\nContact:\n(+86) 0512-36658756 (Monday-Friday, 09:00-17:00)\ndkulibrary@dukekunshan.edu.cn\nNo. 8 Duke Avenue, Kunshan, Jiangsu Province, China 215316\n\nThis page is about the Kunshan campus library. It is not Duke University Libraries in Durham, North Carolina.\n\nSource: https://library.dukekunshan.edu.cn/locations-hours/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)\n\nDKU Library Guide (January 2025 brochure)\n\nThis document copies service hours and space facts from the January 2025 DKU Library Guide PDF. Where it disagrees with the later Locations & Hours website, treat the website as current and this brochure as dated January 2025.\n\nLibrary building: Monday-Sunday 08:00-23:00. Side gates use swipe access. The guide lists 23 self and group study rooms and 560 seats.\n\nnot list DKU class dates, DKU library hours, or Wuhan University library hours.\n\nSource: https://www.dukekunshan.edu.cn/about/welcome-to-duke-kunshan-university/ (retrieved 2026-09-10)", "judge_sufficient": true, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "dku", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T203115/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "accepted", "item": 34}
{"run_id": "20261010T203043_0b147ded", "stage": "first_pass", "question": "Who owns Kestrel Aero Components?", "answer": "I do not know based on the retrieved documents.", "evidence": "Kestrel Aero Components — about (fictional shop)\n\nKestrel Aero Components is a made-up job shop in the invented town of Red Mesa. It is not a real aerospace supplier.\n\nHangar 2 machines titanium. Shop 6 machines aluminum. The traveler office is in Hangar 2, bay C.\n\nFay Aerospace (sister shop, not Kestrel)\n\nFay Aerospace is a made-up composites shop across the highway. Its only mill is a 3-axis router. Fay does not hold lot KX-441.\n\nDo not treat Fay hours or specs as Kestrel's.\n\nQuality registration\n\nKestrel is registered to AS9100D. It is not registered to ISO 13485. The quality office is the glass room in Hangar 2.\n\nKestrel contacts\n\nTraveler desk: 555-2201. Quality office: 555-2202. Email: travelers@kestrel-aero.example\n\nOfficer names are omitted on purpose.", "judge_sufficient": false, "judge_supported": true, "human_sufficient": null, "human_supported": null, "notes": "", "corpus": "kestrel", "source_run": "experiments/output/20261010T202849/eval_guided/traces", "sample_stratum": "recovery_trigger", "item": 35}
